    "note": "Today against a month ago. The belly has moved most — the three-year is up 16.32% over the month, the two-year 16.23%, the five-year 15.10% — and every maturity from two years out now yields 5% or more. Reported closes on Thursday were about 4.94% on the two-year, 5.21% on the ten and 5.49% on the thirty; the source table prints 4.87%, 5.18% and 5.47%, which is what the curve above draws. Next week's supply is bills only; the ten-year and thirty-year auctions land on 7 and 8 October.",
